  (text "A couple of notes after building:\nIf you power this board through the rectifier diodes\nEither by AC or by DC current, while the raspberry pi is not docked\nwith the 40 pin header, you can run your finger along the GPIO pins\nand make the relays buzz. Scary the first time it happened to me\nSecond, you should probably figure out how to safely manage \na capacitor of this size. Pull down resistor or something like that?"
    (at 107.3912 94.5388 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 5d0849f3-3081-4fc2-821a-3a6cdafe3cf0)
  )
  (text "Something got messed up here.\nThe zone 5 diode/relay isn't connected to the 5V rail\nLook at the schematic and see the other zone relays are connected to 5V"
    (at 88.2396 164.1348 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 5d450c78-f03f-4c91-b0ee-e63a4e498d33)
  )
  (text "Full Bridge Rectifier to turn 24VAC to about 24VDC"
    (at 136.2964 106.2736 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid c6f7a0ba-b902-483f-8a8b-77afcf7a6a5b)
  )

